proposed_api_examples:
Examples (JSON payloads customers send to Redwood when creating a route):

1) Pin by tag (best for human-readable pins maintained by model authors):
{
  "model_pin": {
    "type": "tag",
    "value": "stable-2026-03"
  }
}

2) Pin by exact semver:
{
  "model_pin": {
    "type": "semver",
    "value": "1.4.2"
  }
}

3) Pin by semver range (compatible updates allowed):
{
  "model_pin": {
    "type": "semver-range",
    "value": ">=1.4.0 <2.0.0"
  }
}

4) Pin to a source commit id (strongest, immutable):
{
  "model_pin": {
    "type": "commit",
    "value": "3f9d8a2b7e1c9f6d..."
  }
}

Server will return the resolved model reference in responses under resolved_model = {"id": "<canonical-version-id>", "origin": "tag|semver|commit", "matched_value": "..."}.

Note: Above examples are textual; SDKs will provide typed helpers rather than requiring customers to construct raw objects.
